        },
        "body": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "text": "<p>Every KRAMÈ trouser begins not in a factory, but in a wardrobe that wasn't working — too many trousers for too many versions of one woman's day. We looked to India's handloom tradition for the answer. Each idea takes shape in the hands of artisan weavers, men and women whose craft has been passed down through generations, now at risk of disappearing. Rooted in that heritage yet designed for modern movement, every trouser becomes more than a garment — it is trust, placed once again in the hands that wove it.</p>"
          }
        },
